---
title: DungeonForge — OOP & Design Patterns UML
---
classDiagram
direction LR

%% ============================================================
%% DUNGEONFORGE CLASS DIAGRAM
%% Pattern labels are intentionally explicit and styled:
%% Strategy, State, Command, Observer, Decorator, Abstract Factory,
%% Factory Method + Template Method, Singleton, Simple Factory,
%% Composite (macro command), and Memento (turn snapshot).
%% ============================================================

namespace Core {
  class Entity {
    <<abstract>>
    #String name
    #int hp
    #int maxHp
    #int attackPower
    #int defense
    +isAlive() bool
    +takeDamage(amount)
    +heal(amount)
    +describe()* String
  }
  class Player {
    -int gold
    -int xp
    -List~Item~ inventory
    -Weapon equippedWeapon
    +equip(Weapon) Weapon
    +getAttackPower() int
    +lifesteal() int
  }
  class Monster {
    -String species
    -int xpReward
    -CombatStrategy strategy
    -MonsterState stateName
    +setStrategy(CombatStrategy)
    +setState(MonsterState)
    +hpFraction() double
  }
  class Combat {
    -EventBus bus
    +monsterTurns(Player, Room)
    +playerStrikes(Player, Monster)
    -monsterActs(Monster, Player, Room)
  }
  class GameWorld {
    -Player player
    -MonsterFactory monsterFactory
    -ThemeRegistry themes
    -List~DungeonLevel~ levels
    -generate()
    -populatorFor(ThemeKit, boolean) RoomPopulator
  }
  class DungeonLevel {
    -int depth
    -String themeName
    -List~Room~ rooms
  }
  class Room {
    -String id
    -String flavor
    -List~Monster~ monsters
    -List~Item~ floorItems
    -Chest chest
    -Map~String,Room~ exits
  }
}
Entity <|-- Player : inheritance
Entity <|-- Monster : inheritance
GameWorld *-- "1..*" DungeonLevel : composition
DungeonLevel *-- "1..*" Room : composition
Room o-- "0..*" Monster : contains
Room o-- "0..*" Item : floor loot
Room o-- "0..1" Chest : contains
GameWorld --> Player
GameWorld --> MonsterFactory
GameWorld --> ThemeRegistry
Combat --> Room
Combat --> Player
Combat --> EventBus

namespace Strategy_Pattern {
  class CombatStrategy {
    <<interface>>
    <<Strategy>>
    +chooseAction(Monster, Player, Room) Action
    +name() String
  }
  class AggressiveStrategy {
    <<ConcreteStrategy>>
    +chooseAction(...) Action
  }
  class HealerStrategy {
    <<ConcreteStrategy>>
    +chooseAction(...) Action
  }
  class RangedStrategy {
    <<ConcreteStrategy>>
    +chooseAction(...) Action
  }
  class SkittishStrategy {
    <<ConcreteStrategy>>
    +chooseAction(...) Action
  }
  class RedCoatStrategy {
    <<ConcreteStrategy>>
    +chooseAction(...) Action
  }
  class Action {
    <<Decision DTO>>
    -Type type
    -Entity target
    -String flavor
    +wait(flavor)$ Action
  }
}
CombatStrategy <|.. AggressiveStrategy
CombatStrategy <|.. HealerStrategy
CombatStrategy <|.. RangedStrategy
CombatStrategy <|.. SkittishStrategy
CombatStrategy <|.. RedCoatStrategy
Monster o-- CombatStrategy : has-a / runtime swappable
CombatStrategy ..> Action : returns decision
Combat ..> Action : executes decision
note for CombatStrategy "STRATEGY: interchangeable combat algorithms. Monster holds a strategy by composition and can swap it at runtime; strategies decide, Combat acts."

namespace State_Pattern {
  class MonsterState {
    <<interface>>
    <<State>>
    +canAct() bool
    +damageMultiplier() double
    +next(Monster, Player) MonsterState
    +label() String
    +onEnter(Monster)
  }
  class IdleState {
    <<ConcreteState>>
  }
  class HuntingState {
    <<ConcreteState>>
  }
  class EnragedState {
    <<ConcreteState>>
    +DAMAGE_BONUS$
  }
  class FleeingState {
    <<ConcreteState>>
    +DAMAGE_DEFICIT$
  }
  class DeadState {
    <<ConcreteState>>
  }
  class GameState {
    <<interface>>
    <<State>>
    +onEnter(GameContext)
    +onExit(GameContext)
    +availableCommands() List~String~
    +name() String
    +isTerminal() bool
  }
  class ExploringState
  class InventoryState
  class CombatState
  class GameOverState
}
MonsterState <|.. IdleState
MonsterState <|.. HuntingState
MonsterState <|.. EnragedState
MonsterState <|.. FleeingState
MonsterState <|.. DeadState
Monster o-- MonsterState : current lifecycle state
IdleState ..> HuntingState : next()
HuntingState ..> EnragedState : health threshold
HuntingState ..> FleeingState : health threshold
EnragedState ..> FleeingState : health threshold
MonsterState ..> DeadState : death transition
GameState <|.. ExploringState
GameState <|.. InventoryState
GameState <|.. CombatState
GameState <|.. GameOverState
GameContext o-- GameState : current game state
note for MonsterState "STATE: lifecycle-dependent behavior (can act, damage multiplier, transitions). Distinct from Strategy: state answers WHEN/how lifecycle affects behavior; strategy answers HOW to choose a combat action."

namespace Factory_Patterns {
  class MonsterFactory {
    <<Simple Factory>>
    -Map~String,MonsterDef~ blueprints
    +createMonster(id) Monster
  }
  class MonsterDef {
    <<Blueprint data>>
    +String id
    +String name
    +int hp
    +int attack
    +int xp
    +String theme
    +String strategy
  }
  class ThemeKit {
    <<interface>>
    <<Abstract Factory>>
    +createMonster(...) Monster
    +createBoss(...) Monster
    +createLoot(depth) Item
    +createRoomFlavor() String
  }
  class CryptThemeKit
  class ForgeThemeKit
  class FrostThemeKit
  class WinterfellThemeKit
  class ThemeRegistry {
    <<Registry / kit selector>>
    -MonsterFactory monsterFactory
    +forDepth(depth) ThemeKit
  }
  class RoomPopulator {
    <<abstract>>
    <<Template Method + Factory Method>>
    #ThemeKit theme
    +populate(Room, depth) final
    #createEncounter(depth)* List~Monster~
    #createChest(depth) Chest
    +kind()* String
  }
  class StandardRoomPopulator
  class TreasureRoomPopulator
  class BossRoomPopulator
}
MonsterFactory ..> MonsterDef : loads JSON blueprints
MonsterFactory ..> Monster : creates
ThemeKit <|.. CryptThemeKit
ThemeKit <|.. ForgeThemeKit
ThemeKit <|.. FrostThemeKit
ThemeKit <|.. WinterfellThemeKit
ThemeRegistry --> ThemeKit : selects family
ThemeRegistry --> MonsterFactory
GameWorld --> ThemeKit : requests theme family
RoomPopulator <|-- StandardRoomPopulator
RoomPopulator <|-- TreasureRoomPopulator
RoomPopulator <|-- BossRoomPopulator
RoomPopulator o-- ThemeKit : delegates product family
RoomPopulator ..> Room : populates
RoomPopulator ..> Monster : encounter products
RoomPopulator ..> Chest : optional chest
note for ThemeKit "ABSTRACT FACTORY: creates a consistent family of themed products (monsters, bosses, loot, room flavor)."
note for RoomPopulator "TEMPLATE METHOD: final populate() fixes the algorithm's order. FACTORY METHOD: subclasses decide createEncounter(); optional createChest() is a hook."
note for MonsterFactory "SIMPLE FACTORY idiom (explicitly not a GoF pattern in source): centralizes Monster construction from data-driven blueprints."

namespace Command_Pattern {
  class Command {
    <<interface>>
    <<Command>>
    +execute()
    +undo()
    +getDescription() String
    +endsTurn() bool
    +isUndoable() bool
  }
  class AbstractCommand {
    <<abstract>>
    #GameContext ctx
    +execute()
    +undo()
  }
  class AttackCommand
  class DropCommand
  class EquipCommand
  class EnchantCommand
  class UseItemCommand
  class TakeCommand
  class MoveCommand
  class SimpleCommand
  class NoCommand
  class MacroCommand {
    <<Macro Command / Composite>>
    -List~Command~ children
    +execute()
    +undo()
  }
  class CommandParser {
    -CommandFactory factory
    +parse(line, ctx) Command
  }
  class CommandFactory {
    <<interface>>
    <<Factory / registry>>
    +create(...) Command
  }
  class CommandHistory {
    -Deque~Command~ undoStack
    -List~String~ replayLog
    +push(Command)
    +undoLast() bool
  }
  class GameContext {
    <<Command Receiver Context>>
    -GameWorld world
    -Player player
    -EventBus bus
    -Combat combat
    -CommandHistory history
    -GameState state
    +syncState()
  }
}
Command <|.. AbstractCommand
Command <|.. SimpleCommand
Command <|.. NoCommand
AbstractCommand <|-- AttackCommand
AbstractCommand <|-- DropCommand
AbstractCommand <|-- EquipCommand
AbstractCommand <|-- EnchantCommand
AbstractCommand <|-- UseItemCommand
AbstractCommand <|-- TakeCommand
AbstractCommand <|-- MoveCommand
Command <|.. MacroCommand
MacroCommand o-- "1..*" Command : contains / composites
CommandParser --> CommandFactory
CommandParser ..> Command : parses text into object
CommandFactory ..> Command : creates
AbstractCommand --> GameContext : receiver
CommandHistory o-- Command : undo stack and replay
GameContext --> GameWorld
GameContext --> Player
GameContext --> Combat
GameContext --> EventBus
note for Command "COMMAND: encapsulates a request as an object so it can be executed, logged, replayed, and potentially undone."
note for MacroCommand "COMPOSITE applied to commands: one command contains a list of commands. Undo executes children in reverse order."
note for CommandHistory "History stores command objects for undo and descriptions for replay. TurnSnapshot supplies captured before-state for undo."

namespace Memento_Pattern {
  class TurnSnapshot {
    <<Memento>>
    -captured player and world state
    +capture(...)
    +restore(...)
  }
}
TurnSnapshot ..> Entity : records/restores HP
TurnSnapshot ..> Room : records room state
TurnSnapshot ..> Player : records inventory/equipment
Command ..> TurnSnapshot : undo support
note for TurnSnapshot "MEMENTO: captures enough prior turn state to restore it without exposing snapshot internals to ordinary game flow."

namespace Decorator_Pattern {
  class Item {
    <<interface>>
    +getName() String
    +getWeight() double
    +getValue() int
    +describe() String
  }
  class Potion
  class Armor
  class Treasure
  class Hourglass
  class Chest {
    -List~Item~ contents
    +add(Item)
    +getContents() List~Item~
  }
  class Weapon {
    <<interface>>
    +getDamage() int
    +lifesteal() int
  }
  class BasicWeapon
  class WeaponDecorator {
    <<abstract>>
    <<Decorator>>
    #Weapon wrapped
    #prefix()* String
    #valueBonus()* int
    +getDamage() int
    +lifesteal() int
    +getName() String
    +getValue() int
    +unwrap() Weapon
  }
  class FlamingWeapon
  class FrostWeapon
  class KeenWeapon
  class VampiricWeapon
  class EnchantmentRegistry {
    <<Decorator factory / registry>>
    +decorate(Weapon, enchantment) Weapon
  }
}
Item <|.. Potion
Item <|.. Armor
Item <|.. Treasure
Item <|.. Hourglass
Item <|.. Weapon
Weapon <|.. BasicWeapon
Weapon <|.. WeaponDecorator
WeaponDecorator <|-- FlamingWeapon
WeaponDecorator <|-- FrostWeapon
WeaponDecorator <|-- KeenWeapon
WeaponDecorator <|-- VampiricWeapon
WeaponDecorator o--> Weapon : wraps / delegates
Player o-- Item : inventory
Player o-- Weapon : equipped weapon
Chest o-- "0..*" Item : contents
EnchantmentRegistry ..> WeaponDecorator : stacks decorators
note for WeaponDecorator "DECORATOR: wraps a Weapon behind the same interface, delegates existing behavior, and adds/changes selected properties. Decorators can be stacked."

namespace Observer_Pattern {
  class EventBus {
    <<Subject / Publisher>>
    -List~GameEventListener~ listeners
    +subscribe(GameEventListener)
    +unsubscribe(GameEventListener)
    +publish(GameEvent)
  }
  class GameEventListener {
    <<interface>>
    <<Observer>>
    +onEvent(GameEvent)
  }
  class GameEvent {
    -EventType type
    -Map~String,Object~ data
  }
  class EventType {
    <<enumeration>>
  }
  class QuestTracker
  class AchievementSystem
  class CombatLog
  class DangerMeter
  class DamageMeter
  class ConsolePrinter
  class Quest
}
GameEventListener <|.. QuestTracker
GameEventListener <|.. AchievementSystem
GameEventListener <|.. CombatLog
GameEventListener <|.. DangerMeter
GameEventListener <|.. DamageMeter
GameEventListener <|.. ConsolePrinter
EventBus o-- "0..*" GameEventListener : subscriptions
EventBus ..> GameEvent : publishes
GameEvent --> EventType
GameEventListener ..> GameEvent : receives
QuestTracker o-- Quest
QuestTracker --> EventBus : completion messages
Combat --> EventBus : publishes combat events
note for EventBus "OBSERVER: publishers depend on the event contract, not concrete listeners. New listeners can subscribe without changing Combat."

namespace Singleton_Pattern {
  class GameConfig {
    <<Singleton>>
    -static GameConfig instance
    -Map~String,Object~ settings
    -GameConfig()
    +getInstance()$ GameConfig
    +getInt(key) int
    +getDouble(key) double
    +resetForTests()$
  }
  class RandomSource {
    <<Singleton>>
    -static RandomSource instance
    -Random rng
    -long seed
    -RandomSource()
    +getInstance()$ RandomSource
    +reseed(seed)
    +nextDouble() double
    +pick(options) T
    +resetForTests()$
  }
  class Json {
    <<utility>>
    +parseObject(text)$ Map
  }
}
GameConfig ..> Json : reads config
RandomSource --> GameConfig : obtains seed
GameWorld ..> GameConfig
Combat ..> GameConfig
MonsterFactory ..> GameConfig
note for GameConfig "SINGLETON: private constructor and static accessor enforce one shared settings instance. Source notes global-state/testing tradeoffs."
note for RandomSource "SINGLETON: one seeded RNG keeps dungeon generation reproducible across runs and tests."

%% Relationships across pattern boundaries
Main ..> GameWorld : builds world
Main ..> CommandParser : input / script loop
Main ..> CommandHistory : records commands
Main ..> EventBus : wires observers
Combat ..> CombatStrategy : asks for action
Combat ..> MonsterState : checks lifecycle and transitions
Player ..> Weapon : damage / lifesteal polymorphism
ThemeKit ..> Item : creates themed loot
ThemeKit ..> Monster : creates themed monsters

